  <data name="rtbInformation.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>       𝗜𝗻𝘁𝗿𝗼𝗱𝘂𝗰𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻

Open Shelf is a library management system that allows admins and members to manage books, members, and library operations efficiently.

____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

        𝗙𝗲𝗮𝘁𝘂𝗿𝗲𝘀

• Separate roles for Members and Admins.
• Member Login &amp; Registration system.
• Admin Login &amp; Registration system.
• Add, Remove, View Books functionality.
• Issue and Return Books with availability tracking.
• View Members Info and borrowing history.
• Generate secure passwords for members.
• Dashboard navigation for easy access to all system functions.
• Identifiers (Member ID, Library ID, First/Last Name) for tracking records.
• User-friendly Windows Forms interface.

____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________


             𝗙𝗼𝗿𝗺𝘀

Member Login Form : Log members into the system or register new members.

• Sign In: Use this button to log in with existing Member ID and password.
• Sign Up: Use this button to register a new member in the LMS database.
• Exit: Use this button to close the login form.

Add Books : Add new books to the library with all required details.

• Add Book: Save the book to the database.
• Exit: Return to the dashboard.

Admin Login Page : Log administrators into the system.

• Login: Access the dashboard with admin credentials.
• Exit: Return to previous screen.

Admin Registration : Register a new admin account.

• Register: Save new admin details.
• Exit: Return to login page.

Issue Books : Main control panel to access all library functions.

• Login Page: Open the login interface.
• View Members Info: See details of registered members.
• Issue Books: Open the issue book form.
• Return Books: Open the return book form.
• View Books Info: View book details.
• Info: View system information.
• Setting: Access system settings.
Identifiers: First Name, Last Name, and Library ID are used to identify a member.

Member Login Page : Log members into the system.

• Sign In: Log in using Member ID and password.
• Sign Up: Register a new member.
• Exit: Close the login form.

Member Registration : Register a new library member.

• Register: Save member details to the database.
• Generate: Automatically create a secure password.
• Exit: Close the registration form.

Remove Books : Remove books from the library database.

• Remove Book: Delete the selected book.
• Exit: Close the form.

Remove Members : Remove members from the system.

• Remove: Delete the selected member.
• Exit: Close the form.

Return Books : Record returned books and update availability.

• Return Book: Record a book return.
• Issue Book: Go to the issue book form.
• Log Out: Log out from the system.
• Exit: Close the form.

View Books Info : Display all books with details and availability.

• Add Books: Go to the Add Book form.
• Remove Books: Go to the Remove Book form.
• Exit: Close the form.

View Members Info : Display all members and their borrowing history.

• Add Members: Go to the registration form.
• Remove Members: Go to the remove members form.
• Exit: Close the form.

